  "verification": [
    "All indexed routes and identities resolve; explicit prerequisite/next edges are acyclic, reasoned and optional. Same-name point-group and Lie lessons remain distinct.",
    "The graph loads only for learning views. Local chapter changes update it without changing course-render behavior; stale async callbacks cannot expose a lab graph.",
    "The original official band and companion structure files retain their exact SHA-256 and full BSD license. Real frequencies, q-point order, path segmentation, eigenvectors and selected mode flow through public calculation entries.",
    "Length and frequency declarations preserve provenance, distinguish explicit user confirmation, and reject inconsistent units. Frozen-mode export converts declared au lattice lengths into Angstroms.",
    "SPT entropy retains the original natural-log numeric field and adds nat/bit metadata and conversion. Density-matrix entropy retains its original log2/bit numeric field.",
    "All four pathway families retain raw valid or incomplete drafts through actual course-tab handlers. Valid inputs do not produce a false schema warning; incomplete fields identify their own validation error. Ordinary tab navigation does not run a calculation.",
    "Thirty-four additional optional connections come from substantive reading of 21 existing lessons, their exercises, declared models and bounded operation panels. All destinations resolve and the combined graph remains acyclic. Links retain polar/axial action spaces, energy-unit choices, finite layer-normal boundaries, and the distinct geometry and response refinement grids.",
    "Forty-eight further optional connections preserve the preceding 82 and connect 47 previously index-only lessons. Every one of the 197 registered lesson panels renders its exact native prerequisite and next hrefs, including overflow links. That intermediate 130-edge graph is retained in full, all visible reasons have English translations, and every newly connected lesson is exercised through the actual classroom shell without calculation or mastery-state access.",
    "Visible reasons distinguish ordinary frequency and input-cell thermal normalization, tensor intrinsic symmetry and engineering shear, SI Boltzmann moments and device absorption, arbitrary pairing scales and NS eV, fractional and radian Bloch momentum, and GT copy gauges versus dimension-reduced 6j/9j tables. These are preparation recommendations, not automatic transfer of numeric results between different models.",
    "Forty-two further optional transfers preserve all preceding 130 edges and connect 36 previously index-only lessons. The 172-edge graph over 148 connected lessons is acyclic; all 197 native lesson routes and every prerequisite/next href are checked, with complete English reasons and the actual classroom shell exercised for all 36 new identities.",
    "Visible reasons retain proper-rotation lift limits, complete double-group versus representative counts, antiunitary conjugation and same-momentum conditions, ordinary versus magnetic settings, and SO(3) versus generalized O(3). Structural reasons distinguish angstrom geometric amplitudes from dimensionless Landau coordinates, positive diffraction phases, per-input-cell quasiharmonic energies and Cp, reduced scalar walls versus independent eV SSH chains, and meV spin-wave energies with different magnetic-cell momentum intervals.",
    "Eighty-seven further read optional relationships preserve all preceding 172 edges and connect the remaining 49 named inventory lessons. All 197 lessons now have recommendations through 259 acyclic edges. Tests lock every new pair and identity, all native lesson links, complete English reasons, 142 real classroom-shell contexts and 46 independent expert entries without calculation or mastery-state access.",
    "New visible boundaries retain equal-input-frequency SHG j/k symmetry without full Kleinman permutation, χ versus piezoelectric e and d=χ/2, reciprocal fractions versus radian wavevectors, exact complex amplitudes versus fixed-irrep path spaces, single-particle versus Slater determinant models, electric versus magnetic probes and their separate units/thermal weights, same-k antiunitary tests, complete fermionic exchange, and declared order-parameter manifolds.",
    "The water lesson links to a GaAs displacement comparison. Both editions check the rigid rotation against all three fcc primitive directions. The optical contrast uses the existing Python phonon example geometry and a verified model frame. The exact trace.txt lookup opens the ordinary and magnetic band-character tool with its existing input constraints.",
    "Every indexed lesson opens contextual course search from its current learning panel. All 197 canonical lesson identities resolve into 51 topics. Same-name lessons stay distinct. Users can browse their topic or retain the query when broadening to the course catalog or the whole lesson inventory.",
    "Both search indexes retain all 1651 BNS and OG pairs. Full numbered lookups select the matching magnetic group, including through a delayed or retried catalog. Gamma mode diagnostics recover all rigid-translation weight from the original GaAs acoustic triplet and split it equally between two unchanged T2 labels after a controlled mixing.",
    "Atlas material cards open their declared lessons and preserve material-specific lab inputs. Atlas workbench links record the selected group and valid reciprocal-space conventions when the browser history entry is created.",
    "The GaAs exercise compares the same Gamma calculation for two synthetic presets, with explicit manual runs. Switching back restores the earlier official phonon inputs and their confirmed units.",
    "The homepage, atlas and finder share exact group-number lookup. The introductory screw-axis and Lie lessons open the cases used in their worked examples. The silicon atlas and bilingual catalog reach the local QE–Si evidence page through a standard link.",
    "The representation workbench menu and calculation action resolve exact SG, BNS and OG identifiers against the current catalog. Exact symbols take precedence over partial matches. Alias selections preserve the current momentum and spin when they refer to the same group.",
    "The introductory fourfold comparison uses a common rotation and starting point. The P 4, P 4₁ and P 4₃ representatives return to the same wrapped point and accumulate 0, 1 and 3 axial cells after four steps. Exact ordinary space-group symbols with spaces, numerical subscripts or underscores resolve across the finder, atlas and workbench.",
    "The foundations preview compares one and two actions for C₄(z) and σ(xz) on xy and xyz. Exact lesson links retain the verified beginner basis and give the xz mirror convention used for the water displacement character.",
    "The shared finder and calculation directory match declared CIF and POSCAR filename patterns and the CONTCAR alias. Choosing the structure tool leaves the file selection and conversion to the user.",
    "The finder and calculation directory resolve explicit bilingual little-group, double-valued and antiunitary search terms. Explicit symbolic terms lead to the exact solver. The numerical workbench preserves its current group, momentum and spin setting and waits for a calculation request."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All 197 indexed lessons have at least one reviewed optional connection in the 259-edge graph. This coverage records concrete conceptual transfers; it does not establish complete operational teaching depth, targeted diagnosis or an authentic scientific workflow in every lesson.",
